Date: Tue, 12 Jun 2012 22:38:20 +0000
Subject: How to run mapreduce job on multiple cores?
Message-ID: <nT90CLVyJgk.6sFdBXYwu4gJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhipe/c/nT90CLVyJgk/m/6sFdBXYwu4gJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each node in my cluster has 16 cores, I set the parameter
mapred.tasktracker.map.tasks.maximum <- 16. However I only see two of
the cpus are used at about 100% level on each node by the top
command . The memory usage is about 14% on each thread. How can I
utilize multiple cores to speed up the mapreduce job? Very appreciate
any of your help.

From u5b0c9158bfa781ba at groups.google.com  Wed Jun 13 21:58:21 2012
From: u5b0c9158bfa781ba at groups.google.com (Saptarshi Guha)
Date: Wed, 13 Jun 2012 21:58:21 +0000
Subject: Re: [rhipe] How to run mapreduce job on multiple cores?
Message-ID: <nT90CLVyJgk.AKYB6nZIu1oJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <nT90CLVyJgk.6sFdBXYwu4gJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
References: <nT90CLVyJgk.6sFdBXYwu4gJ@rhipe.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhipe/c/nT90CLVyJgk/m/AKYB6nZIu1oJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mapred.tasktracker.map.tasks.maximum is a site wide configurtion and
wont change per job.
Probably mapred.tasktracker.map.tasks.maximum is 2 in your
hadoop-site.xml? or something similar.

