Hi, I was wondering if there were any results from testing this.

Also, I found out that if I set up the input data such that there is one line of data per file, then hadoop will run as many mappers as there are input files (which is what I want). However, there are a total of ~200,000 different input lines. I don't know if HDFS or even a regular filesystem can support that many files in a single directory, and in any event that seems kind of cumbersome. Is there a way to reorganize my code so that I don't have to have all these individual output files, each containing one line?

(I haven't tried producing all 200,000 input files. I don't know if it will really create 200,000 mappers or just intelligently send the data in round-robin fashion to a smaller cluster of mappers. I don't really want 200,000 mappers but I do want each line of input to be processed in isolation. )

Thanks,
Dan

